@startuml activity_qa
!include _theme.iuml
title End-to-end question answering workflow
start
:User enters question, mode, strategy,\ntop-k and max hops;
if (mode?) then (open-domain)
  :Search Wikipedia (question + question entities);
  if (Wikipedia reachable?) then (no)
    :Return HTTP 503 with explanation;
    stop
  endif
  :Fetch articles -> sections -> chunks;
  :Find bridge entities in best passages;
  :Fetch bridge articles (hop 2);
  :Build in-memory corpus (embed, NER, FAISS, BM25, graph);
else (multi-document)
  if (processed documents exist?) then (no)
    :Return HTTP 409 "upload documents first";
    stop
  endif
  :Use persistent corpus snapshot;
endif
:Compute semantic, BM25 and hybrid scores;
:Rank passages (FAISS / BM25 / hybrid);
:Extract and match question entities;
:Build question subgraph\n(seeds + multi-hop expansion);
:Enumerate evidence chains\n(simple paths, cutoff = max hops);
:Graph heuristic scores (PPR + chain support);
if (trained GNN checkpoint?) then (yes)
  :GAT reranking + chain rescoring;
else (no)
  :Fall back to graph heuristic (noted in response);
endif
:Select evidence (top chain + top passages);
:Generate answer (Flan-T5 -> reader -> extractive);
if (answer grounded in evidence?) then (no)
  :Reject answer;
endif
:Validate citations (support per claim);
:Compute confidence from measured signals;
if (similarity, coverage, entity grounding,\nanswer support and confidence OK?) then (yes)
  :Return answer, fact/inference steps,\nevidence chain, citations, scores;
else (no)
  #FFF3CD:Return "Insufficient evidence found to answer\nthis question reliably." + reasons;
endif
:Persist query, answer, citations, timings, subgraph;
stop
@enduml
